[h1]ZeD-GUI [B42] | tester build 0.2.0-t1[/h1]
[b]This is a test build.[/b] It's unlisted, so you're here because someone sent you the link. Thank you for playing it. Problems go in the pinned [b]Bug reports[/b] discussion, one post per problem.

Every window, the HUD and the menus, rebuilt from scratch for Build 42. It looks like a Mac from 1993 because that's the computer we wanted to survive the apocalypse on. It plays with a controller as well as with a mouse and keys.

[h2]Before you subscribe[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Build 42 only.[/b] Built and tested on 42.21. It won't run on Build 41.
[*][b]Play a new game or a copy of a save.[/b] It's a test build. Keep your real saves safe.
[*][b]Single player is where it's been tested.[/b] Multiplayer hasn't been. If you try it on a server, tell us how it went.
[*][b]It replaces vanilla's windows.[/b] Mods that add their own buttons to vanilla's inventory or character window won't show those buttons, because those windows are hidden. Mods that use the game's own systems (context menu options, container buttons, items, recipes) work.
[*][b]It adds one item:[/b] a steel digital watch in the loot. Take ZeD off mid-save and those watches go with it. Everything else is interface, and safe to add or remove.
[*][b]English for now, ready for other languages.[/b] Wherever the game already has the words, ZeD uses the game's own translation. The rest of ZeD's text sits in one file for translators.
[/list]

[h2]What you get[/h2]
[b]Your window and the world's window.[/b] Your stuff on one side: loot, what you wear, health, temperature, who you are, your journal, skills, the radio you carry. The world on the other: loot, crafting (at any bench or station near you), building, maps, foraging, animals, the radio nearby, the vehicle you're next to, furniture. Roll either side up into its title bar when you only need the other.

[b]Cards for everything.[/b] Click an item, a generator, a campfire, a farm plot, a trough, a padlock, a liquid: you get one card with what it is, what you can do and why you can't yet.

[b]The HUD.[/b] Your hands and hotbar on a belt. A watch you actually use. A dashboard when you drive. Moodles where you want them. A bar over your head that says what you're doing and how long the queue is (or just ten little lights, if you'd rather).

[b]Maps.[/b] Survey, color or the old paper road map, with the flyers you've read pinned on it. Your notes are the game's own map notes, so they show on every map.

[b]The menus.[/b] The main menu is a desk with a CRT on it. Load, new game, mods, options, sandbox, character creation, server settings: all ZeD windows on that screen, with the game's own logic underneath.

[b]Controller.[/b] Everything you can do with a mouse, you can do with a pad. D-pad moves between things, A and B are left and right click, X and Y open things.

[b]Your colours.[/b] Dark, light or high contrast, nine accents, two text sizes, a UI scale for big screens.

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe.
[*]Main menu, Mods: turn on [b]ZeD-GUI[/b]. Put it after other interface mods in the load order.
[*]Start a new game, or play a copy of a save.
[*]Options, Mods, ZeD-GUI: pick your theme, accent, text size, scale, where the moodles sit and how much the action bar says.
[*]Your inventory key opens your window. Your loot key opens the world's. On a controller, the same buttons as vanilla.
[/olist]
Big screen (1440p, 4K)? Leave UI scale on Auto, or set it yourself in the same place.

[h2]Something broke[/h2]
Post in the pinned [b]Bug reports[/b] discussion, not the comments. Comments scroll away, discussions don't. Tell us:
[list]
[*]The version: 0.2.0-t1 (it's also in Mods, and in the desk's ZeD menu under About).
[*]Your game version and your mod list.
[*]What you did, what you expected, what happened. A screenshot helps more than words.
[*]Your console.txt: [i]C:\Users\(you)\Zomboid\console.txt[/i] on Windows, [i]~/Zomboid/console.txt[/i] on Linux and macOS. The game replaces it every time it starts, so copy it before you restart. Put it on a paste site and post the link.
[/list]
[b]If ZeD stops you from playing:[/b] turn on Options, Mods, ZeD-GUI, [b]Safe mode[/b]. The game's own screens come back and you can keep playing. Say so in your report.
Play without the [i]-debug[/i] launch option unless we ask for it. With it, the game stops on every Lua error, other mods' too.

[h2]For server admins[/h2]
Mod ID: ZeD_UI
Every player needs it, since it adds an item.

